{"parentUuid":"42c8a044-ca65-4033-81a7-bd677fe7663e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4V5iNQVuoVs6L4quygb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Context:** Session focused on fixing the Windows laptop's broken backup situation, discovered via a `RECOVERY-INVENTORY.md` commit that arrived from the Windows machine mid-session.\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- Read and summarized `~/.claude/RECOVERY-INVENTORY.md`: Windows laptop has **no working backup**. ~15 GB exists in single copy only (SportScienceResearchRepo 4.37 GB, Football 2.94 GB, Risk_Stratification_Engine 1.80 GB, ForcePlate_DecisionSystem 1.69 GB, `~/.codex` history). All 131 repos, `~/.claude`, skills, global memory, and Google Drive docs are safe.\n- Three root causes: (1) all nine KeystoneOS Windows scheduled tasks are **Disabled** — switched off during the Mac move, never restored; (2) two replacement tasks were registered with **no trigger** — they show `Ready` forever and will never fire; (3) the Windows backup manifest is actually the **Mac's manifest** (all `/Volumes/CRASHBOX` and `/Users/kristinarash/...` paths), last state written 2026-08-14 status ERROR.\n- Corrected an error in the recovery report: it claimed the backup scripts in `DEV\\_INBOX\\` weren't in any repo because `dev-sync` skips underscore folders. False — `dev-sync` only skips `.claude`, `_tools`, `_DRIVE`, `token-dashboard`, `*_OLD_merged*`. `_INBOX` is its own repo (`github.com/erash11/_INBOX`), clean and pushed. Its fix #2 is unnecessary.\n- User asked twice for clarification on \"the Windows file\" — wording was ambiguous; it's an instruction page to follow, not an executable.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Chose option A: fix scripts on the Mac now and hand Windows a paste-ready page, rather than waiting until next on Windows. Rationale: edits are safe from here; turns the Windows session into one paste instead of a debug job.\n- Changed `~/DEV/_INBOX/backup_dev.ps1` from `/MIR` to `/E` — mirroring propagates accidental deletions into the backup. (`backup_ai_sessions.ps1` was already `/E`.)\n- Created `~/.claude/scripts/backup-manifest.windows.json` — real Windows destinations. Explicitly noted inside the file that **nothing reads it yet**; it is documentation until a Windows checker exists.\n- Do NOT move the backup scripts out of `DEV\\_INBOX\\` — the registered scheduled task points there; moving them breaks the task.\n- Do NOT re-enable the nine KeystoneOS Windows tasks. `~/.claude/scripts/daily-backup.ps1` was overwritten by the Mac version on 2026-08-05 (rsync + Mac paths); the original Windows one is frozen at `daily-backup.ps1.win-orig`.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- `schtasks /Change` cannot add a schedule to a task that has none — must use `Set-ScheduledTask` with a trigger array.\n- `G:` (Google Drive) is a **per-user mount**. A task running as SYSTEM sees no `G:` and writes nothing, silently.\n- A fixed-time trigger on a laptop that sleeps never fires. Fix: pair a time trigger with `-AtLogOn` plus `-StartWhenAvailable` so missed slots catch up.\n- Verification must confirm **bytes landed in Google Drive**, not that the task looks healthy — that's the gap the whole recovery report traces back to.\n- Cross-machine push collisions: three separate pushes arrived from the Windows laptop during this session, each requiring a merge. Worth knowing whether something is running unattended over there.\n- A commit \"apply global skill audit\" (12:12 today, authored by user, from the other machine) deleted 913 files, cutting skills from ~160 to 63, and wrote `project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md`. Applied and pushed on the Mac. Appears deliberate; git retains every deleted skill if recovery is needed.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- **On Windows:** run `/dev-sync`, then follow `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\_INBOX\\FIX-WINDOWS-BACKUP.md` — core fix is `Set-ScheduledTask` with triggers for \"Backup DEV to Drive\" (Weekly Sun 6pm + AtLogOn) and \"Backup AI Sessions to Drive\" (Daily 5:30pm + AtLogOn), in PowerShell 7 as admin, logged in as the user. Verify `NextRunTime` shows a date, then confirm files actually appeared in Google Drive.\n- **Confirm the skill audit was intentional** — if not, investigate; nothing is lost either way.\n- **`/backup` still has not been run** — CRASHBOX SSD backup outstanding from this morning's list.\n- Earlier flagged: `project_settings-json-bom-trap.md` rewritten to cover BOM + mangled characters affecting `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` too, not just `settings.json`; `MEMORY.md` index line updated. Committed and pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41893,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1821,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41893,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1821,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41893},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011Cf4V5hbn1jPCwcY2TF177","type":"assistant","uuid":"1fcd2301-57fb-4a5e-9690-d4ed43ca971a","timestamp":"2026-09-15T03:05:49.241Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler","sessionId":"9c1fe48d-8404-456e-b65e-61c070870312","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"session-start-progressive-disclosure"}
